{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["וסחרוה — the letter het takes a qamatz, and likewise from the root גאל: גְּאָלַנִי; from שחט: וַיִּשְׁחָטוּהוּ; from שאל: וישאלוני — משפטי צדק. From בחר: בחרוהו. From פעל: יפעלוהו."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {0 "The lemma וסחרוה (Genesis 34:10) shows a qamatz under the het where one might expect a shva; Rashbam explains this as a regular phonological pattern in guttural-letter verbs, illustrating with comparable forms. The citation משפטי צדק (Job 36:17) apparently supports the form וישאלוני (qamatz in the syllable before the guttural)."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:46:12.790087786Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}